From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:00:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] common: the PS4's thread names go to the app's runtime

Thread names were dropped on the PS4 (pthread_rename_np isn't a system
call a homebrew app makes there). They now go to the runtime the app
links (ps4_watch_thread, weak): its hang reports name each thread, and
its busy threads (the emulated CPU cores, the GPU thread) get heap
arenas of their own instead of all sharing the one locked heap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
---
 src/common/thread.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/thread.cpp b/src/common/thread.cpp
index a1e3f7882..45b07653d 100644
--- a/src/common/thread.cpp
+++ b/src/common/thread.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@
 #include "common/string_util.h"
 #include "common/windows/timer_resolution.h"
 #else
+#ifdef __OPENORBIS__
+extern "C" __attribute__((weak)) void ps4_watch_thread(const char* name); // the PS4 app's runtime
+#endif
 #if defined(__FreeBSD__) && !defined(__OPENORBIS__) // the PS4 has neither header
 #include <sys/cpuset.h>
 #include <sys/_cpuset.h>
@@ -519,8 +522,11 @@ void SetCurrentThreadName(const char* name) {
 #elif defined(__HAIKU__)
     rename_thread(find_thread(NULL), name);
 #elif defined(__OPENORBIS__)
-    // The PS4: pthread_rename_np isn't among the system calls a homebrew app makes there.
-    (void)name;
+    // The PS4: pthread_rename_np isn't among the system calls a homebrew app makes there. The name
+    // goes to the app's runtime instead (port/ps4_sampler.cpp): hang reports name the thread, and
+    // the busy ones get a heap arena of their own.
+    if (ps4_watch_thread)
+        ps4_watch_thread(name);
 #elif defined(__Bitrig__) || defined(__DragonFly__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__)
     pthread_set_name_np(pthread_self(), name);
 #elif defined(__NetBSD__)
